Package: MRKCFC
Type: Package
Title: Multivariate Robust K-Centers Functional Clustering for Sparsely Observed Longitudinal Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Bingbing", family = "Fan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "bingbingfan24@hotmail.com"),
    person(given = "Rou", family = "Zhong", role = "ctb",
           comment = "KFPCA-derived implementation"),
    person(given = "Jingxiao", family = "Zhang", role = "ctb",
           comment = "KFPCA-derived implementation")
    )
Description: Multivariate K-centers functional clustering (MKCFC) and its robust
    form (MRKCFC) for sparsely and irregularly observed multivariate longitudinal
    data that may be non-Gaussian. Each class is described by a two-stage
    multivariate functional principal component analysis, a marginal analysis of
    each variable followed by an eigendecomposition of the stacked scores, and
    subjects are reassigned to the class that reconstructs their trajectories
    best. The robust form uses Kendall's tau functional principal component
    analysis in the first stage and a spatial-sign scatter matrix in the second,
    so that neither stage needs a moment assumption on the principal component
    scores. The package also carries the cluster-validity criteria, metrics and
    data-generating functions used by the accompanying manuscript; the study
    scripts that call them are distributed separately
    <https://github.com/BingbingFan/MRKCFC_Simulation>.
    Includes an internal KFPCA-derived implementation based on KFPCA version 2.0
    by Rou Zhong and Jingxiao Zhang <https://github.com/BingbingFan/KFPCA>,
    incorporated under GPL (>= 3). MRKCFC-specific adaptations are by Bingbing
    Fan and are identified in the source.
URL: https://github.com/BingbingFan/MRKCFC
